[38;2;124;124;124mmutually disjoint perfect matchings in the complete graph $K_\omega$, where [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$K_\omega$ is the complete graph on an infinite set of vertices.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$K_\omega$ is the complete graph on a countably infinite set of vertices. A [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mperfect matching in $K_\omega$ is a set of edges such that every vertex is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mincident to exactly one edge in the matching. Since the vertex set is countably [0m[38;2;124;124;124minfinite, a perfect matching partitions the vertices into pairs (2-element [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msubsets).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe question: what is the largest number of mutually disjoint (edge-disjoint) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mperfect matchings we can have?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFirst, let me think about the edge count. $K_\omega$ has countably many [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mvertices, so it has countably many edges (since $\binom{\omega}{2} = \omega$). [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mEach perfect matching uses countably many edges (one per vertex, so $\omega/2 = [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\omega$ edges). So the maximum number of edge-disjoint perfect matchings is at [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmost $\omega$ (countably many), since the total number of edges is countable and[0m[38;2;124;124;124meach matching uses infinitely many.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, can we achieve $\omega$ (countably infinitely many) mutually disjoint [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mperfect matchings?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me think about this more carefully. The question is about the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcardinality. The answer should be a cardinal number.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about the finite case first. $K_{2n}$ has $2n$ vertices and $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\binom{2n}{2} = n(2n-1)$ edges. Each perfect matching has $n$ edges. So the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmaximum number of edge-disjoint perfect matchings is at most $2n-1$. In fact, [0m
